# Whether a >=1-year kidney recipient (KALT_STATUS_CALC == 2) gets their own
# post-transplant time-varying switch, the same way <1-year recipients do.
#   FALSE = >=1-year recipients are coded as "waitlist/dialysis" for their
#           ENTIRE follow-up in the time-varying model. Internally consistent
#           with Group as a fixed label, but it puts real post-transplant
#           person-time into the reference state.
#   TRUE  = >=1-year recipients also switch state at THEIR OWN kidney TX date,
#           using the same interval cutpoints as <1-year recipients. Nobody who
#           is ever transplanted stays labeled "waitlist" forever.
#
# [F6] Set to TRUE, and under KALT_MAX_DAYS = Inf this is now MANDATORY rather
# than preferable. Both timing strata are one KALT arm ([K1]), so the >=1-year
# recipients are inside the exposure -- and the ONLY thing standing between that
# merge and a fabricated result is that their exposure starts when their kidney
# does.
#
# The magnitude, recomputed from this pipeline's own output: median
# liver-TX-to-kidney-TX delay among those 1,467 patients is 1,467 days (4.0
# years, IQR 1.5-9.0), 67.5% of their post-liver-TX follow-up precedes their
# kidney transplant, and 0 of their 213 deaths occur before it -- necessarily,
# since you must be alive to be transplanted. Fixed-labelling them KALT from
# time zero injects ~8,385 event-free person-years into the KALT arm and turns
# what the old <365-day definition showed as a null (85.6% vs 87.5% at 5 years,
# log-rank p=0.19) into a manufactured 14.5-point advantage (78.4% vs 92.9%,
# p<0.001). Setting this FALSE while KALT_MAX_DAYS is Inf reproduces exactly
# that artifact; Section 24.1 refuses the combination rather than fitting it.
#
# Making the switch time-varying instead puts each late recipient's pre-kidney
# years in the reference state, where they belong, and answers the same
# question without the artifact. It also fixes Table 4's power problem: the
# post-transplant intervals go from 4-19 events each (several below
# TABLE4_MIN_EVENTS_PER_INTERVAL, forcing adaptive merges) to 25-85 events
# each, so all nine intervals are estimable at full granularity.
#
# CONSEQUENCE TO KEEP IN MIND: Block 2's reference state means "not yet
# transplanted at this instant," while Block 3's fixed-Group contrast means
# "never received a kidney at all." Under KALT_MAX_DAYS = Inf these are much
# closer than they used to be -- Block 3's "LTA" arm is now true LTA rather than
# a mixture -- but they are still not identical, because Block 2's reference
# additionally holds every KALT patient's own pre-transplant person-time.
# Section 24.6's footnote says so explicitly. Section 29's S29_LATE_TX_HANDLING inherits this
# setting and becomes "switch" automatically, which is the intended pairing --
# its Panel A/Panel B split already documents the same fixed-vs-time-varying
# distinction.
TABLE4_LATE_TX_TIME_VARYING <- TRUE

