# respectively) were WRONG (they are actually Hep B cirrhosis, Hep B+D
# cirrhosis, and alcoholic+HCV combined). Corrected below.
#
# Notably, OPTN has a SINGLE DEDICATED CODE for "alcoholic cirrhosis with
# hepatitis C" (4216) -- the DGN_TCR/DGN2_TCR secondary-diagnosis combination
# logic this section used to derive that category is unnecessary and has
# been removed; a direct code lookup is both simpler and correct.
#
# Two judgment calls, flagged rather than silently decided:
#   - "Alcoholic cirrhosis" folds in 4217/4218/4219 (acute alcoholic
#     hepatitis / acute alcohol-associated hepatitis / alcohol-associated
#     cirrhosis without acute hepatitis) alongside 4215 (plain "alcoholic
